      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "The International Court of Justice has ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya people.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "On 19 November 2026, the court found that Myanmar committed acts falling under the genocide convention, with an intent to destroy a substantial part of the Rohingya population in Myanmar.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386740487:3"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "The case is titled The Application of the Convention on the Prevention and Punishment of the Crime of Genocide (The Gambia v. Myanmar).",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1386740487:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "On the map, the International Court of Justice is in the Netherlands, where the reports place it.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "The report was filed by AFP.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:2026-11-19:18"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:41Z",
      "text": "Al Jazeera headlined its coverage, \"ICJ to rule on Rohingya genocide case against Myanmar.\"",
      "cites": [
        "news:aljazeera:f19b9dd52ab6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "France 24 asked, \"Myanmar's Rohingya case: how does the ICJ define genocide?\"",
      "cites": [
        "news:france24:783277d01e65"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-19T00:00:53Z",
      "text": "DW headlined its report, \"Myanmar committed genocide against Rohingya, top UN court rules.\"",
      "cites": [
